WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.402
-Hi, everybody. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:05.138
As we did last night, I'm going
to turn over the top of our show

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.207
to "Late Night" writer
Amber Ruffin.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.309
The crisis we're going through
is at its heart about anger

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:12.311
and frustration
in the Black community

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.981
over years of mistreatment
by law enforcement.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:18.551
So here is Amber
with another story.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.353
-Last night, I told you a story

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.722
about an encounter I had
with police.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.658
Now let me tell you
another story.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.529
One time, a few years ago,
I was living in Amsterdam.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.197
And I flew to Chicago
for the weekend

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.965
to visit some friends
who live there.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:36.703
When I got there, my friend Jeff
and I hopped in his car

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.739
and headed out to pick up
our friend Krasney,

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.207
who just so happened to live

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:45.811
next to the alley
behind the police station.

00:00:45.811 --> 00:00:47.914
So, Jeff parks his car

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.116
at the gas station
at the end of the alley

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.685
so that I can run out,
go pick up Krasney,

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.121
and take her back to the car.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.358
I'm freaking thrilled.
I hadn't seen her in years.

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:02.261
So, we were all going to
go have dinner and catch up.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:04.697
Now, I get out of the car
and go down the alley.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.700
And because Jeff is watching me,
I skip down the alley

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.269
to her house to make him laugh,
you know?

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:12.504
But little did I know

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:15.975
skipping down a police-station
alley is a big no-no.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.545
Because I end up
skipping towards a cop car

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:21.547
that's driving at me
down the alley.

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:23.249
The sirens go off.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.251
A cop gets out,
and his gun is drawn.

00:01:26.251 --> 00:01:28.421
And he goes, "Put your hands
on the hood of the car!

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.756
Put your hands on the hood!"

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.426
This man is furious.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:37.663
I comply,
and his partner pats me down.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:40.066
Now, this man is livid.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.968
It makes no sense.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:46.105
His anger level towards me
is insane.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:49.408
I am a young, adorable, delight

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:51.510
literally skipping
down the street,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.579
and I've infuriated him.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:57.883
So, this man asked me,
"Where are you coming from?"

00:01:57.883 --> 00:02:00.219
And I go, "Amsterdam."

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.688
Now, this answer enrages him.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:04.691
And he goes, "No, where are you
coming from right now?

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.292
Where are you coming from?"

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:11.464
And I go, "From the airport.
From a flight. From Amsterdam."

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.499
And he goes, "Why in the world

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.701
are you running down
this alley?!"

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:18.537
I go, "I'm not running.
I'm skipping.

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.239
I'm happy to be back in town.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.776
I'm going to pick up
my friend Krasney

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.711
and take her back to Jeff's car,

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.880
and we're all going to
go catch up over dinner."

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.017
And I remember,
"Oh, thank God. Jeff is here."

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.218
I gesture back to Jeff.

00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:37.724
Jeff is standing outside of his
car just watching all of this.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:43.396
And he goes --
So, the cop and I see Jeff.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:46.766
And thank God Jeff
didn't come running up to us,

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.402
because he could have
gotten us both shot.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:53.673
But the cop sees that Jeff,
a white man, has seen all this,

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:59.078
and he changes his attitude
with the quickness.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:02.181
He's suddenly professional
instead of antagonistic.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:06.318
And he tells me
that I was wrong for running.

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:09.755
And it takes everything in me
not to tell him

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:13.059
that if I wanted
to run down the alley,

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:16.095
that would be perfectly legal.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.430
So, instead,
I also gently remind him

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.733
that I was not running,
I was skipping.

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:23.736
So, the cop gets in his car,
and he leaves.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:27.540
And I walk to Krasney's house.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.610
I get her.
We take her back to the car.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.746
Jeff is really bothered
by what happened, but I'm not.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.583
[Bleep] That man could have
shot me in a second.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:40.119
People who know me would be
running around talking about,

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.654
"Attacking an officer
doesn't seem like

00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:46.291
something Amber would do,
but the officer said she did,

00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:49.462
so that has to be
what happened."

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:53.633
So...

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.869
The second I see Krasney,
I feel a lot better.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:04:00.339
And we go, and we have
a lot of fun that night.

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:03.742
And if you think about it, it's
kind of my duty to have fun

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:10.082
because at any time, I could
get murdered by the police.

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:16.222
Now, every Black person I know
has stories like that.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.890
[ Sighs ]

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.793
It's crazy that people don't
run around telling everyone

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.294
these stories all the time.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.429
But there's this unspoken rule

00:04:24.429 --> 00:04:28.100
that Black people are
supposed to take it in stride.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.471
Can you imagine having
someone pull a gun on you

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:36.175
and being expected
to take it in stride?

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:41.848
Now imagine a bunch of incidents
like that over one lifetime,

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:45.618
multiply that by
43 million African-Americans,

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:49.555
and that is why things
are like this right now.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.323
That is why people are angry.

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:55.662
And if you're not angry...
why not?

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.598
-Thank you, Amber.

